# MobileDeck repository-wide ignores.
# Parts of the tree have their own .gitignore (for example android/.gitignore);
# this file covers what is shared, plus the host's build output and the runtime
# state the agent writes on a developer machine.

# --- Go build output ---------------------------------------------------------
# `go build -o mobiledeck ./cmd/mobiledeck` inside host/. The release binary is
# a build artefact, never committed.
host/mobiledeck
host/mobiledeck.exe
host/*.test
host/*.out
coverage.out
coverage.html

# --- Android -----------------------------------------------------------------
build/
.gradle/
.kotlin/
local.properties
*.apk
*.aab
captures/
.cxx/
.externalNativeBuild/

# --- Runtime state and secrets ----------------------------------------------
# Written by the agent at runtime and machine-local. devices.json and
# audit.jsonl are secrets; see docs/SECURITY.md §6.
devices.json
audit.jsonl
logs/
tls/
config.json

# Throwaway config directory used by scripts/dev-host.sh and
# scripts/dev-host.ps1.
.devdata/

# Config directory bind-mounted into the optional agent container by
# docker-compose.yml (./data:/data). Machine-local runtime state, never
# committed.
#
# The leading slash is load-bearing. An unanchored `data/` matches at every
# depth, so it also swallowed the Android client's main package directory
# (android/app/src/main/java/dev/mobiledeck/data/) — already-tracked files kept
# working, but the next new file added there was ignored silently and would have
# been missing from every clone. Anchor it to the repository root; do not
# shorten it back to `data/`.
/data/

# --- Editor and OS noise -----------------------------------------------------
.idea/
.vscode/
*.iml
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Build output of the optional end-to-end recording window
# (scripts/smokeinput). It is a test fixture, not a shipped artefact.
scripts/smokeinput/smokeinput
scripts/smokeinput/smokeinput.exe
